        "original_id": "0fd67ae0-c7ee-55bc-aa30-6de39785b661",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Cleek-McCabe Site, Walton, Boone County, Kentucky, Bluegrass region, northern Bluegrass region\n- Concepts: Middle Fort Ancient culture, archaeological sites, geographic regions\n\nFacts:\n- The Cleek-McCabe Site is an archaeological site associated with the Middle Fort Ancient culture from 1200 to 1400 CE.\n- The Cleek-McCabe Site is located near Walton in Boone County, Kentucky, in the northern Bluegrass region.\n- The Bluegrass region, called Eskippakithiki in Shawnee, is a geographic region in the U.S. state of Kentucky.\n- The Bluegrass region makes up the northern part of Kentucky, where most of the state's population has lived and where its largest cities developed.",
